SUMMARY:Resistance and rebellion: A people’s history of the Canadian
  state study series - by International Socialists
LOCATION:427 Bloor St W.
DESCRIPTION:More info: https://www.socialist.ca/node/5260\n\nHosted by
  International Socialists (https://www.socialist.ca/)\n\nIn 1983 a general
  strike movement swept British Columbia. Months of protests against the
  provincial government coalesced into a general strike involving 85\,000
  workers. Instead of proceeding with the strike\, union leadership called
  it off. Join for a discussion of the inspiring story of Operation
  Solidarity and its betrayal by the union leadership.
END:VEVENT
